For normalization:
```python
def norm(s):
    s = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s or '')
    s = s.lower()
    s = re.sub(r'\\[a-zA-Z]+', ' ', s)  # LaTeX macros
    s = re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9 ]+', ' ', s)
    return re.sub(r'\s+', ' ', s).strip()
```
Title similarity: difflib.SequenceMatcher on norm strings; ledger titles may be truncated (the CSV showed truncated titles like "The Exterior Solution" — actually row SRC-002 title was "Naked Singularities for the Einstein Vacuum Equations: The E..." truncated to 60 chars in display only because I sliced. In CSV, is the full title stored? Earlier print sliced to 60. Fine.)

